his information is only used for _display_ purposes: it in no way affects any of the arithmetic of the contract, including {IERC20-balanceOf} and {IERC20-transfer}."},"decreaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically decreases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address. - `spender` must have allowance for the caller of at least `subtractedValue`."},"deposit(address,uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"amount to deposit*","_lsdToken":"token to deposit"}},"getComposition()":{"returns":{"_0":"list of compositions for each lsd"}},"getCompositionTargets()":{"returns":{"_0":"list of composition targets"}},"getDepositRoom(address)":{"params":{"_lsdToken":"address of token"},"returns":{"_0":"deposit room for token*"}},"getFees()":{"returns":{"_0":"list of fees"}},"getLSDTokens()":{"returns":{"_0":"list of strategies"}},"getRewards()":{"returns":{"_0":"total rewards","_1":"total fees*"}},"getSharesByStake(uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"staked amount"},"returns":{"_0":"amount of shares*"}},"getStakeByShares(uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"shares amount"},"returns":{"_0":"amount of stake*"}},"getWithdrawalAmounts(uint256)":{"details":"sender receives an amount of each lsd proportional to the size of the deposit gap between each lsd's pre-withdrawal composition and its post-withdrawal target composition (as a result, the current composition will move closer to the target after each withdrawal)","params":{"_amount":"amount to withdraw"},"returns":{"_0":"list of lsd amounts*"}},"increaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically increases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address."},"name()":{"details":"Returns the name of the token."},"owner()":{"details":"Returns the address of the current owner."},"proxiableUUID()":{"details":"Implementation of the ERC1822 {proxiableUUID} function. This returns the storage slot used by the implementation. It is used to validate that the this implementation remains valid after an upgrade. IMPORTANT: A proxy pointing at a proxiable contract should not be considered proxiable itself, because this risks bricking a proxy that upgrades to it, by delegating to itself until out of gas. Thus it is critical that this function revert if invoked through a proxy. This is guaranteed by the `notDelegated` modifier."},"removeLSDToken(address,uint256[])":{"params":{"_compositionTargets":"basis point composition targets for each remaining lsd*","_lsdToken":"address of token"}},"renounceOwnership()":{"details":"Leaves the contract without owner. It will not be possible to call `onlyOwner` functions anymore. Can only be called by the current owner. NOTE: Renouncing ownership will leave the contract without an owner, thereby removing any functionality that is only available to the owner."},"setCompositionEnforcementThreshold(uint256)":{"details":"the composition enforcement threshold is the total amount of deposits required for composition targets to be enforced (if the threshold was 10000 and the targets for 2 lsds were 70% and 30%, up to 7000 of the first lsd could be deposited even if there were no deposits of the second lsd but after 7000 is reached, enough of the second lsd would have to be deposited to open up more room for the first lsd)","params":{"_compositionEnforcementThreshold":"threshold total deposit amount*"}},"setCompositionTargets(uint256[])":{"params":{"_compositionTargets":"list of basis point composition targets*"}},"setCompositionTolerance(uint256)":{"details":"the composition tolerance is the percentage swing that any lsd can have from its composition target in either direction (if the composition tolerance was 50% and an lsd had a composition target of 30%, then its minimum composition of the pool is 15% of deposits and its maximum is 45%)","params":{"_compositionTolerance":"basis point composition tolerance*"}},"setPaused(bool)":{"params":{"_isPaused":"pause status of the contract*"}},"setWithdrawalFee(uint256)":{"params":{"_withdrawalFee":"fee in basis points*"}},"sharesOf(address)":{"params":{"_account":"account address"},"returns":{"_0":"account's share balance*"}},"symbol()":{"details":"Returns the symbol of the token, usually a shorter version of the name."},"totalSupply()":{"returns":{"_0":"total supply"}},"transfer(address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transfer}. Requirements: - `to` cannot be the zero address. - the caller must have a balance of at least `amount`."},"transferFrom(address,address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transferFrom}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. This is not required by the EIP. See the note at the beginning of {ERC20}. NOTE: Does not update the allowance if the current allowance is the maximum `uint256`. Requirements: - `from` and `to` cannot be the zero address. - `from` must have a balance of at least `amount`. - the caller must have allowance for ``from``'s tokens of at least `amount`."},"transferOwnership(address)":{"details":"Transfers ownership of the contract to a new account (`newOwner`). Can only be called by the current owner."},"updateFee(uint256,address,uint256)":{"params":{"_feeBasisPoints":"fee in basis points*","_index":"index of fee","_receiver":"receiver of fee"}},"upgradeTo(address)":{"details":"Upgrade the implementation of the proxy to `newImplementation`. Calls {_authorizeUpgrade}. Emits an {Upgraded} event."},"upgradeToAndCall(address,bytes)":{"details":"Upgrade the implementation of the proxy to `newImplementation`, and subsequently execute the function call encoded in `data`. Calls {_authorizeUpgrade}. Emits an {Upgraded} event."},"withdraw(uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"amount to withdraw*"}}},"title":"Liquid Staking Derivative Index Pool","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"addFee(address,uint256)":{"notice":"adds a new fee"},"addLSDToken(address,address,uint256[])":{"notice":"adds a new liquid staking derivative token"},"balanceOf(address)":{"notice":"returns an account's stake balance"},"deposit(address,uint256)":{"notice":"deposits lsd tokens and mints lsd index tokens"},"getComposition()":{"notice":"returns the current basis point composition of deposits"},"getCompositionTargets()":{"notice":"returns a list of basis point composition targets for each lsd"},"getDepositRoom(address)":{"notice":"returns the deposit room for an lsd token"},"getFees()":{"notice":"returns a list of all fees"},"getLSDTokens()":{"notice":"returns a list of all supported lsd tokens"},"getRewards()":{"notice":"returns the amount of rewards earned since the last update and the amount of fees that will be paid on the rewards"},"getSharesByStake(uint256)":{"notice":"returns the amount of shares that corresponds to a staked amount"},"getStakeByShares(uint256)":{"notice":"returns the amount of stake that corresponds to an amount of shares"},"getWithdrawalAmounts(uint256)":{"notice":"returns the amount of each lsd a withdrawer will receive for an amount of index tokens"},"removeLSDToken(address,uint256[])":{"notice":"removes a liquid staking derivative token"},"setCompositionEnforcementThreshold(uint256)":{"notice":"sets composition enforcement threshold"},"setCompositionTargets(uint256[])":{"notice":"sets composition targets"},"setCompositionTolerance(uint256)":{"notice":"sets composition tolerance"},"setPaused(bool)":{"notice":"pauses/unpauses the contract"},"setWithdrawalFee(uint256)":{"notice":"sets the withdrawal fee"},"sharesOf(address)":{"notice":"returns an account's share balance"},"totalSupply()":{"notice":"returns the total supply of staking derivative tokens"